arospkg 0.4.0
=============

Install software with apkg in the Shell or PkgManager on the desktop.

INSTALL
-------

1. Unpack the archive for your CPU and ABI.
2. Close PkgManager and let any apkg operation finish.
3. In the Shell, enter the unpacked drawer and run:

     Copy apkg C:
     apkg --version
     apkg update

Keep your existing SYS:Packages when upgrading. Versions 0.3.x need this
manual copy to reach 0.4.

PkgManager is included in the x86_64 ABIv11 archive. Keep the unpacked
drawer and start it from there with:

     Run PkgManager

Click Update index, select a package and click Install. Open folder takes
you to the installed program. Start it from its icon.

BUILDS
------

0.4.0:
  x86_64-aros-v11    apkg and PkgManager
  i386-aros-v0       apkg
  aarch64-aros-raspi apkg for native AROS on Raspberry Pi, ABIv1

Experimental mainline x86_64 ABIv1 and hosted Macaros aarch64 builds remain
available in release 0.3.1. Pi and Macaros builds are separate.

Downloads: https://github.com/tomaszstaniak/arospkg/releases

x86_64 ABIv11 has the most test coverage, on AROS One 1.3 under QEMU.
The i386 archive was checked through update, search, install, open and
removal. The Pi build was checked with a local catalogue and cached
archives under QEMU raspi3b; network operations were not tested.

For online operations you need working networking and the certificate
bundle ENV:SYS/Certificates/ca-bundle.crt. PkgManager needs Zune.

START HERE
----------

  apkg search game        find packages
  apkg show soliton       view details and requirements
  apkg install soliton    download, verify and install
  apkg open soliton       open the installed drawer in Wanderer
  apkg list               list installed packages
  apkg remove soliton     remove it, keeping changed and additional files

Packages go into SYS:Packages by default. To use another root, put it
before the command:

  apkg --root "Work:Packages" install soliton
  apkg --root "Work:Packages" open soliton

Use the same root for later operations on those packages.

NEW IN 0.4
----------

- Open folder in PkgManager and apkg open.
- Package notes after installation and in the details.
- Clearer operation stages, results and removal reports.
- Larger catalogues: tested with 5,000 packages on x86_64 ABIv11.
  The parser allocates as needed, within memory and size limits.
- apkg self-update, with the previous executable kept as apkg.old.

UPDATES
-------

  apkg update                refresh the catalogue
  apkg upgrade <id>          install a newer packaging revision
  apkg rollback <id>         restore the previous revision
  apkg self-update --check   check for a newer stable apkg
  apkg self-update           replace the apkg executable you started

Upgrade supports revisions of the same upstream version, not a change
to a different upstream version. Rollback needs the previous archive
in the cache. Close the application before either operation or removal.

Self-update keeps apkg.old beside the updated executable. PkgManager
must be updated separately from the release archive. Recovery instructions:
https://github.com/tomaszstaniak/arospkg/blob/main/docs/self-update.md

FILES AND RECOVERY
------------------

  SYS:Packages/<id>/       installed program
  SYS:Packages/db/         installation records; do not edit
  SYS:Packages/cache/      downloaded archives

Removal keeps files you changed and files apkg did not install, and lists
them. A later install will not overwrite a drawer left behind by removal.
Move it aside first, keeping any files you need.

  apkg verify <id>         check installed files without repairing them
  apkg doctor              report unresolved operations
  apkg doctor --retry      retry recovery after an interruption

MORE OPTIONS
------------

  apkg --help             common commands
  apkg --help-all         full user help
  apkg --help-testing     diagnostic and test options

--plain removes decorations. --verbose shows more transport and path
details. --json provides machine-readable output for supported commands.
--dry-run previews install, remove, upgrade or rollback without changing
installed files; --fetch permits downloading the archive for that preview.

PkgManager provides the PKGMANAGER ARexx port while it is running.
Examples are in Examples/ARexx. The command reference is at:
https://github.com/tomaszstaniak/arospkg/blob/main/docs/arexx.md

LIMITS
------

- CPU and ABI matching is not proof that every application works.
- System requirements are checked, but dependencies are not installed
  automatically. Installer scripts and shared system files are not managed.
- Downloads use HTTPS and SHA-256 checks. The catalogue is not signed,
  and a matching hash does not establish an application's safety.

CHECKSUMS AND LICENCES
---------------------

BUILD.txt records the source commit and program hashes. apkg --version
reports the running binary's hash. Archive hashes are in SHA256SUMS on
the matching release page.

